exports[`sessionstart.notify-permissions.sh layers given: [case12] the boot list reads the layered allow set when: [t2] no layer holds a Bash allow then: stdout matches snapshot 1`] = `
"
🐢 bummer dude, no guardrails found 🌊

🐚 no pre-approved bash permissions were found
   │
   ├─ the hook looked in:
   │  ├─ <tmp>/.claude/settings.of.repo.json: absent
   │  ├─ <tmp>/.claude/settings.local.json: absent
   │  ├─ <tmp>/home/.claude/settings.json: absent
   │  └─ <tmp>/.claude/settings.json: absent
   │
   ├─ if this clone should have pre-approved permissions,
   │  check that these files exist and hold valid json.
   └─ fix: to write the repo's allowlist, ask your human to run rhx init at the repo root, in their own shell, then restart the session.

"
`;

